From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] shell32: special folders parse and answer like Windows (2017)

shell32: special folders parse and answer like Windows (2017)

From Wine's todo_wine blocks, which record Windows: ParseDisplayName of
My Computer, the desktop and file system folders leaves pchEaten alone;
a file system folder refuses names that are not file names ("." and "..",
empty elements, a leading backslash, forward slashes); a shell extension
with no attributes in the registry is a folder like My Computer; My
Computer has SFGAO_CANLINK through the desktop and not when asked
directly, and an empty item id list is invalid.
---
